    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter today\u2019s slate with a potent offensive profile, anchored by **Yordan Alvarez** (82.97), whose matchup against a shaky 40.50 xERA arm represents the highest upside on the board. **Christian Yelich** (75.84) and **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (75.71) round out our top-tier plays; **Yelich** benefits immensely from a park factor boost (+14%) and a platoon advantage, while **Crow-Armstrong** remains a primary target due to his elite sprint speed and a high-leverage leadoff spot. **Trea Turner** (71.68) is another standout, particularly against Eisert; his ability to exploit a slow SP delivery makes him an ideal candidate to capitalize on the SB scarcity we prioritize. The high scores for **Gary Sanchez** (66.22) and **Luke Raley** (65.33) further solidify a lineup designed to maximize daily efficiency, provided the \"Lineup Pending\" statuses for **Sanchez**, **Carson Benge**, and **Yelich** confirm as anticipated.\n\nThe most difficult exclusion today was **Nelson Velazquez** (55.59), who despite a massive 0.478 xwOBA, fell short of the threshold required to displace our high-floor starters. While **Velazquez** offers significant pop, the combination of a difficult matchup against Lodolo and the superior situational efficiency scores of middle-infield options like **Colt Keith** (54.20) and **Chase Meidroth** (54.20) tipped the scale away from him. We are also closely monitoring **Dillon Dingler** (43.88); despite a favorable wind-out condition, his score is depressed by a -15% dynamic platoon penalty, making him the most volatile piece of today\u2019s construction. As we manage our game caps, we remain committed to benching non-starters like **Caleb Durbin** and **Casey Schmitt** to prioritize the primary lineup\u2019s cumulative efficiency. **Hyeseong Kim** remains sidelined in the minors, pending further roster movement.",
